  "officialHtml": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw1200.html",
  "prefLabel": "Env-Sw 1203.02 Additional Location Restrictions for Landfills",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Sw 1203.02 Additional Location Restrictions for Landfills.\n\n(a) A permit-by-notification landfill shall not be sited less than 75 feet to surface water or wetlands.\n\n(b) A permit-by-notification landfill shall be located to provide at least 4 feet of vertical separation between the base of the disposal area and the seasonal high groundwater table.\n\n(c) A permit-by-notification landfill shall be located to provide at least 4 feet of vertical separation between the base of the disposal area and bedrock.\n\n(d) A permit-by-notification landfill shall not be sited less than 50 feet from the footprint of any landfill which is not yet capped.\n\n(e) A permit-by-notification landfill having an active life longer than 90 days shall be sited on publicly owned land only.\n\nSource. #6619-B, eff 10-29-97; (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Sw 1200) ss by #8459, eff 10-28-05 (formerly Env-Wm 2903.02); ss by #10595, eff 7-1-14; ss by #13865, eff 2-6-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-sw1200.html"
